Who brings forth a kiss of circumference, the glyphs hooked and loosened and linking, as though they were dancing through moths of minutes and months like windâout of a god whose name is Goneâ...
Fukkit and lukky art thou in the wind moving marjoram into the mint, the fuzz and down of the former grazing the raised ribs of the other, the essences borneâ
Pheromones suddenly wafting, your eye catching the gradient greens and vein-like patterns, the gray stubble of sageâs tongue, thick oreganoâs glister and whorl, stalks of thyme spiking the air on a kitchen porch or Sikinos slope with its lavender flower, lit up, still, in June;
The blue film of nightâs end rolling into white near dawn, the light by which you know a friend, the ancients explain, from six feet offâor, a wolf from a dog;
The glow of morning bougainvillea, its papery bracts in a breeze like prayer, its bezeled ruby beginnings morphing into pinks- and magentas-to-come, cream-tipped corollas on perfect display, style and stigma sheathing the anther;
Then creeping Christiansâ dusky luster, in the shade at noon;
Almonds swelling jade drupes into the sinking summer, encoding springâs initial explosion;
Pomegranateâs garnet, pendant, containingâagainst the green of its arch and stretchâsix hundred seeds dark with light, glinting in its skin;
Fucked, art thou, and lucky, who translates it into the day as blessedâ
So blessÃ¨d as in blasted art thou, in a way, in whom this knowing is strengthened in bringing you down to the cords of arthritic knees, â¨wrestling the gust of a given momentâs givingâlike vaporâand â¨strangely grateful;
